<title>Sore Throat and Pharyngitis (Child): Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0577-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>&#x201C;Hot potato&#x201D; voice or sudden severe illness?</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-2">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Child with sore throat? Apply clinical decision rule (Table 1).</label>
<path target="cell-6">Score 0-1</path>
<path target="cell-5">Score 2-3</path>
<path target="cell-4">Score 4 or 5</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>Treat with penicillin VK (if &lt;27&#x00A0;kg; 250 mg bid or tid; if &gt;27 kg 500 mg bid or tid); amoxicillin may be used as an alternative.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Rapid antigen detection test (RADT).</label>
<path target="cell-4">Positive RADT result</path>
<path target="cell-7">Negative RADT result</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Consider throat culture, if indicated.</label>
<path target="cell-4">Positive throat culture</path>
<path target="cell-6">Negative throat culture</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Supportive care. If symptoms persist or there is prominent fatigue, consider testing for infectious mononucleosis.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-3">
<label>Consider peritonsillar abscess.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
